Subject: Object creation: JSON.parse shape reuse

What this does
  Object creation: JSON.parse shape reuse.

Why we need it
  So every JSON object re-hashes its whole add-transition chain through `add_property`, even though JSON documents repeat the same object layout object after object.

What it adds
  Adds a per-nesting-depth expected-transition cache to the parser: the first object at a depth records its key sequence (`atoms`) and the shape chain it produces; the next object at that depth starting from the same base shape and repeating the same keys adopts each cached shape directly (`json_obj_adopt_shape`, mirroring `add_property`'s matching-shape branch without the hash lookup). A divergence drops the stale tail and rebuilds the chain; duplicate keys fall back to `JS_DefinePropertyValue`; the cache is freed by `JS_ParseJSON_internal` on both paths and re-fetched after each recursive value parse because a nested object can grow the depth-indexed array.

Needs a bytecode version bump
  No.
